ort_id><s:story_id>59553</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Down Cincinnati in Four Sets Friday Evening</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/volleyball-mountaineers-down-cincinnati-in-four-sets-friday-evening</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/volleyball-mountaineers-down-cincinnati-in-four-sets-friday-evening</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Volleyball team sings Country Roads after defeating Cincinnati in four sets on Oct. 16" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/16/DSC08813__1_.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. - The West Virginia University volleyball team (10-7, 3-4 Big 12) defeated Cincinnati, 3-1, on Friday evening at Hope Coliseum, earning its first victory over the Bearcats since 2023 by set scores of 25-21, 25-14, 27-29 and 25-19.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/DSC08813__1_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/DSC08813__1_.jpg"><media:title>WVU Volleyball team sings Country Roads after defeating Cincinnati in four sets on Oct. 16</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/DSC08813__1_.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:55:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59552</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Fall to UCF Friday Afternoon</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/womens-soccer-mountaineers-fall-to-ucf-friday-afternoon</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/womens-soccer-mountaineers-fall-to-ucf-friday-afternoon</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Tyler Clyburn passes the ball during a game at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/16/WVSOCC26_10.16_LH-00181.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 12-ranked West Virginia University women's soccer team fell to UCF, 1-0, on Friday afternoon at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium in Morgantown.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/WVSOCC26_10.16_LH-00181.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/WVSOCC26_10.16_LH-00181.jpg"><media:title>Tyler Clyburn passes the ball during a game at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/WVSOCC26_10.16_LH-00181.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:28:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59551</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Take on Georgia Southern and UAB</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/rifle-mountaineers-take-on-georgia-southern-and-uab</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/rifle-mountaineers-take-on-georgia-southern-and-uab</guid><category>Rifle</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Jacob Wisman competes in the Mountaineers first match of the season" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC07808.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University rifle team is set to take part in two separate matches this weekend on Saturday and Sunday inside the Georgia Southern Shooting Sports Education Center in Statesboro, Georgia. Both days' matches will begin at 8 a.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC07808.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC07808.jpg"><media:title>Jacob Wisman competes in the Mountaineers first match of the season</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC07808.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>8</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59548</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers to Face Maryland Sunday in First Preseason Tuneup</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/mens-basketball-mountaineers-to-face-maryland-sunday-in-first-preseason-tuneup</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/mens-basketball-mountaineers-to-face-maryland-sunday-in-first-preseason-tuneup</guid><category>Men's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="West Virginia coach Ross Hodge observes a preseason practice inside the Basketball Practice Facility earlier this fall." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Hodge-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The first of WVU's three exhibition games will take place Sunday inside the XFINITY Center in College Park, Maryland, when West Virginia takes on the Maryland Terrapins in a 3 p.m. clash streaming live on the Big Ten Network's B1G+.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Hodge-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Hodge-Main.jpg"><media:title>West Virginia coach Ross Hodge observes a preseason practice inside the Basketball Practice Facility earlier this fall.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Hodge-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:09:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>4</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59546</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Open Weekend Hosting Cincinnati for Coal Rush</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/mountaineers-open-weekend-hosting-cincinnati-for-coal-rush</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/mountaineers-open-weekend-hosting-cincinnati-for-coal-rush</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Volleyball played against BYU in its 2025 Coal Rush match" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC00728.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University volleyball team (9-7, 2-4 Big 12) is set to host Cincinnati on Friday, Oct. 16, at Hope Coliseum for a 6 p.m. ET first serve.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC00728.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC00728.jpg"><media:title>WVU Volleyball played against BYU in its 2025 Coal Rush match</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC00728.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:30:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59544</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Cap Homestand Against UCF on Friday</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/womens-soccer-mountaineers-cap-homestand-against-ucf-on-friday</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/womens-soccer-mountaineers-cap-homestand-against-ucf-on-friday</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Layla Thompson dribbles the ball during a match at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC09842.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. (Oct. 15, 2026) – The No. 12-ranked West Virginia University women's soccer team caps a three-game homestand when it welcomes UCF to Morgantown on Friday, Oct. 16. The match is part of a double header with the WVU men's soccer team, and kickoff at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium is set for 3 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC09842.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC09842.jpg"><media:title>Layla Thompson dribbles the ball during a match at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC09842.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:46:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59547</s:story_id></item><item><title>Muller and Syrja Make Finals at ISSF World Cup</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/rifle-muller-and-syrja-make-finals-at-issf-world-cup</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/rifle-muller-and-syrja-make-finals-at-issf-world-cup</guid><category>Rifle</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Lauri Syrja and Oceanne Muller compete at the WVU Rifle season opening event" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Syrja_and_Muller.png" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Oceanne Muller and Lauri Syrja highlighted the Mountaineers in action at the 2026 ISSF World Cup in Cairo, Egypt, as the pair each qualified for one final at the event. Muller competed for France, Syrja for Finland, as Griffin Lake and Ashlyn Blake each competed for the United States.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Syrja_and_Muller.png" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Syrja_and_Muller.png"><media:title>Lauri Syrja and Oceanne Muller compete at the WVU Rifle season opening event</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Syrja_and_Muller.png" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:38:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>8</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59545</s:story_id></item><item><title>West Virginia Set to Host Kentucky</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/mens-soccer-west-virginia-set-to-host-kentucky</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/mens-soccer-west-virginia-set-to-host-kentucky</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Pablo Pozos battles for the ball against South Carolina" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/15/MSOC_VS_USC__61_large.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 24 West Virginia University men's soccer team welcomes Kentucky, Friday, Oct. 16, for a Sun Belt matchup. Kickoff from Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium is set for 7 p.m.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/MSOC_VS_USC__61_large.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/MSOC_VS_USC__61_large.jpg"><media:title>Pablo Pozos battles for the ball against South Carolina</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/MSOC_VS_USC__61_large.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:07:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59543</s:story_id></item><item><title>WVU Falls to No. 1-Seeded Oklahoma State in Playoff Tiebreaker at Big 12 Match Play Championship</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/14/golf-wvu-falls-to-no-1-seeded-oklahoma-state-in-playoff-tiebreaker-at-big-12-match-play-championship</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/14/golf-wvu-falls-to-no-1-seeded-oklahoma-state-in-playoff-tiebreaker-at-big-12-match-play-championship</guid><category>Golf</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Jack Michael lines up a putt" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/14/10142026.GOLF.BIG12.ES.001.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University golf team tied No. 7-ranked and 12-time National Champion Oklahoma State, 2.5-2.5, before falling to the Cowboys in a playoff tiebreaker at the Big 12 Match Play Championship in Salt Lake City on Wednesday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/14/10142026.GOLF.BIG12.ES.001.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/14/10142026.GOLF.BIG12.ES.001.jpg"><media:title>Jack Michael lines up a putt</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/